    {
      "id": "claim_ceb475f6855540f58a6bc62d8955ee07",
      "statement": "All extractors that produce images use the shared get_img_dir() utility which creates per-file subdirectories under temp_dir/images/ using an MD5 hash of the file path and truncated filename stem. PDF formula regions are rendered as cropped PNG images at 200 DPI with 4-point padding around bounding boxes, saved to temp_dir/formulas/<safe_name>/ with degenerate regions (zero/negative dimensions) skipped.",
